The prompt is the overlapping-substring counter. I’m using a recursive implementation whose branches mirror a clean mathematical recurrence, including the otherwise awkward empty-substring case (`len(string) + 1`, matching Python’s range-based interpretation). That shape keeps the K proof about the actual translated AST, while making the induction/circularity argument tractable.
